dotfiles
--------

Minimalist, terminal-first dotfiles repository.

Philosophy: 
  - Use OpenBSD base as much as possible
  - Override defaults only when necessary
  - Terminal-first
  - Portable across BSDs/Linux as far as possible

Choices:
  - Shell:    ksh (POSIX mode, vi bindings)
  - Terminal: xterm with Selenized light color scheme (https://github.com/jan-warchol/selenized)
  - Editor:   vim with minimal highlighting (kind of '4-color philosophy')
  - WM:       cwm (lightweight, keyboard-driven)

Structure:
  .profile .kshrc .exrc        Shell configuration
  .vimrc .vim/colors/4term.vim Editor configuration
  .Xresources                  X11 resources (full 16-color Selenized palette)
  .xsession                    X session startup (xrdb, keymap, TrackPoint, alert monitor)
  .cwmrc                       Window manager configuration
  .local/bin/                  Helper scripts (see below)

Scripts (.local/bin/):
  dotctl    Dotfiles manager (push/pull/status/diff)

Management:
  With supplied tool dotctl:
    Bootstrap from repo root: ./.local/bin/dotctl push
    Then, dotctl should be in the PATH:
      dotctl push    # Update local dotfiles from repo
      dotctl pull    # Update repo from modified local dotfiles
      dotctl status  # Check differences
      dotctl diff    # Show differences
    Options:
      -n  Dry-run (show what would change)
      -f  Force overwrite if destination is newer

  Alternative (manual):
    Copy or symlink files from the repo root to $HOME.
    Ensure ~/.local/bin is in PATH for the scripts.

  Alternative (git bare repo):
    git init --bare $HOME/.dotfiles
    alias dotfiles='git --git-dir=$HOME/.dotfiles/ --work-tree=$HOME'
    dotfiles config --local status.showUntrackedFiles no

